### Rules

1. **Credit me.** If you share it, post about it, or use it in something public, say it was originally made by Matt Burke (emjay045) and link back to:
   `https://github.com/emjay045/ai-memory-cli`
   Don't strip the copyright notice out of the files.

2. **Don't resell it as yours.** You can't take this (or a tiny fork of it) and sell it as your own product, or re-license it and charge for access. Claiming you built it is not cool.

   Using it *inside* something bigger you made is totally fine — like an app or a project that happens to use this for memory. Selling *the library itself* is not.

If you're not sure whether something counts as okay, just ask — I'm pretty chill about it, credit is the only thing I really care about.

### No warranty

This is provided as-is, no guarantees. I'm not liable if something breaks or doesn't work how you expected. Use at your own risk.

